.TH mkfifo 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
mkfifo \- create named pipes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkfifo
.I "name ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkfifo
creates each
.I name
as a FIFO, with mode 0666 less the current
.BR umask .
.PP
A FIFO is a pipe with a name in the filesystem: one process opens it for
writing, another for reading, and data flows between them without either
having to be the other child.  An open for reading blocks until a writer
arrives, and the other way round.
.SH OPTIONS
None; there is no
.BR \-m .
.SH EXIT STATUS
1 if any FIFO could not be created.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mknod (1),
.BR sh (1)
